Zero OS0.7 final three-mode integration verification
2026-11-15 UTC

Exact final ISO
SHA256 6af39753816e30ab40e77cf56af4a8edce4de20abb30ef09d722884c217a5f3b
Size17645568 bytes. The tested private copy and build/zero.iso match.
The parent owns the separate final BIOS64 verification.

Modes: all PASS
BIOS32: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,-lm,-pae, SeaBIOS,128MiB RAM.
UEFI32: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64,-lm, IA32 OVMF4M,128MiB RAM.
UEFI64: QEMU pc/TCG, qemu64, AMD64 OVMF4M,128MiB RAM.
Every mode uses standard VGA and its own writable data, MBR and GPT copies.
UEFI uses private variable stores. The ISO is read-only on IDE index2.
Full commands and VM arguments are retained in run-vms.sh and each mode's
first.commands, first.serial, first.qemu and first.keyboard files.

Inventory and UI
Every boot reached A:|> within40 seconds and showed exactly:
 A:| physical0 raw ZeroFS,1MiB
 B:| physical1 MBR ext4,32MiB, start2048/count65536
 C:| physical1 MBR NTFS,64MiB, start67584/count131072
 D:| physical1 MBR Btrfs,256MiB, start198656/count524288
 E:| physical3 GPT ext4,32MiB, explicitly labelled read-only
The ATAPI optical drive is not exposed as a writable volume.
All three800x600 first.png screenshots were visually inspected: pixel portrait,
desktop, visible terminal, new paths and native worker status are present.
PS/2 entered all62 commands per mode. GO changed roots and absolute reads
selected the requested volume without merging same-named files.
Prompts stay in column0 after LF-only listings; the earlier indentation bug
is resolved. Missing-file and already-exists results do not mark healthy
volumes limited/unavailable in disks.

Filesystem operations: all PASS on each of ext4, NTFS and Btrfs in every mode
Create scratch; save/read mode-specific text; delete scratch; verify missing.
Create same; save/read first contents; overwrite with final contents; attempt
duplicate create and verify existing contents remain; list the root.
Each backend's final same file contains a distinct value:
 MODE ext4 final
 MODE ntfs final
 MODE btrfs final
The separate ZeroFS A:|same contains MODE zero separate. Cross-volume reads
from A confirm all four same names retain independent contents. MODE is
bios32,uefi32 oruefi64. All command responses are checked by the runner.

Read-only enforcement: all PASS
Read/list E:|welcome, then attempt save, create and remove on E. All three
mutations are refused. GO E:| followed by format ZERO is also refused. The
original welcome content is read again. Each complete37,748,736-byte private
GPT image compares byte-for-byte with the immutable fixture afterward.

Threads after disk operations: both counters grow
Mode       Graphics frames       Compute blocks (hex)
BIOS32     01e9 -> 01fa           1227e7 -> 12cddd
UEFI32     01e9 -> 01f9           1255dc -> 130f81
UEFI64     01e1 -> 01f1           257f99 -> 26d7bf
Both workers remain state1. This establishes cooperative thread progress;
it does not claim preemptive scheduling or multiple CPU execution.

Independent filesystem inspection after VM shutdown: all PASS
The runner sends monitor quit and waits for process completion before these
checks. check-filesystems.sh records exact extraction and checker commands.
partx confirms all three MBR extents. Each mode's partition copies were tested:
 e2fsck -fn: exit0
 ntfsfix -n: exit0
 btrfs check --readonly: exit0, no error found
debugfs, ntfscat and btrfs restore independently extract same and match every
expected final byte sequence. Btrfs restore also confirms scratch is absent.
The first/last1MiB gaps, including the MBR, are unchanged. Per-mode checker
logs, readback/expected files and external.status preserve the evidence.
ntfsfix -n is a limited independent consistency check, not Windows chkdsk.

UEFI64 full new-process restart: PASS
After the first VM exited and the external checks completed, a new QEMU
process booted the same ISO using the same private disks/variables. It
rediscovered A-E and read all three final foreign-filesystem contents plus
the separate ZeroFS content. E:|welcome remained unchanged. Root listings,
info and tasks completed. restart.png was visually inspected. The whole
data, MBR and GPT image hashes remain identical to their post-first-run
values, recorded in restart-disks-unchanged.txt. This proves persistence
across a full guest process restart; the restart performs reads, not CRUD.

Preservation and limits
build/data.img and build/data.vdi retain their pre-task hashes. Original
multi-mbr.img/readonly-gpt.img fixtures remain unchanged. inputs.sha256 and
original-inputs-unchanged.txt record this. All four test VM processes, including
the restart, have stopped. No implementation source was changed during these
final tests. The supported filesystems are their explicitly documented bounded
profiles, with flat names and small files; these tests do not establish full
general-purpose ext4/NTFS/Btrfs compatibility. QEMU/firmware/filesystem tools
are external testing dependencies, not guest implementations. Native
VirtualBox execution and physical hardware were not tested here.
